// SR 641.711 — Chapter 11 Implementation
// generated by src/parse.py. Do not edit by hand.

:NOTE
English is not an official language of the Swiss Confederation. This translation is provided for information purposes only and has no legal force.

:INFO
Art. 130 Implementation authorities
1 The FOEN shall implement this Ordinance. Paragraphs 2–9 and Annex 14 number 2.1 remain reserved.
2 The SFOE shall implement the provisions relating to the reduction of carbon emissions from passenger cars, vans and light articulated vehicles. In this it is supported by FEDRO.
3 The FOCBS shall implement the provisions relating to the CO2 levy.
4 The FOEN shall implement:
a. in consultation with the SFOE: the provisions on attestations for domestic emission reductions and increasing the carbon sink capacity and on the promotion of technologies for the reduction of greenhouse gas emissions;
b. in consultation with the SFOE, the State Secretariat for Economic Affairs and the Federal Department of Foreign Affairs: the provisions on the attestations for emission reductions and increasing the carbon sink capacity outside Switzerland.
|

:INFO
Art. 130 (continued)
4bis The SFOE shall implement the provisions on global financial assistance with the long-term reduction of carbon emissions from buildings, on assistance with the direct use of geothermal energy, on assistance for installations producing renewable gases and on assistance for installations using solar thermal energy for process heat.
5 In consultation with the SFOE, the FOEN shall implement provisions relating to the promotion of basic and advanced training.
6 The SFOE and private organisations commissioned by the SFOE or the FOEN shall support the FOEN in implementing the provisions relating to commitments to reduce greenhouse gas emissions.
7 The FOCA shall support the FOEN in implementing the provisions on emissions trading for aircraft operators.
|

:INFO
Art. 130 (continued)
8 It shall enforce the obligation to provide and blend low-emission, renewable and renewable synthetic fuels in accordance with Articles 28f and 28g of the CO2 Act and to fund the measures to reduce greenhouse gas emissions from aviation under Articles 127a–127g.
9 FEDRO is responsible for promoting electric drive technologies in accordance with Articles 129b–129f.
|

